{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2970","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2970","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2970\",\"parent_revision\":\"a32c061bf2f24e54d03d294189d00515b8eaa70a\",\"root_revision\":\"89b061f86273a65e3d7d9418ae2eae9c489345a8cb2b8c46e857f73bb1404978\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBacklog section names are not governed by a single canonical registry. Grooming and review agents each independently choose the section-name string they write to a backlog item, with no shared source of truth and no validation at the write boundary. This allows any agent to introduce an unregistered section name at any time, which is the underlying condition that produced issue #2956 (backlog_groom writes invisible via backlog_view) and remains open after that issue's fix lands, since nothing prevents a future agent from inventing another unregistered section name.\\n\\nThe system must provide one single canonical source of truth listing every legitimate section key and its display heading, used identically for writing and reading sections, so that: every agent that reads or writes a section resolves it through that one registry rather than an independently typed string; deprecated or historic alternate names for a section resolve to the same canonical key through a mapping kept separate from the canonical registry itself; and there is a documented, discoverable convention for how to register a new section when one is legitimately needed, so adding a section is a deliberate, tracked step rather than an implicit side effect of an agent's prompt wording.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: User specified: \\\"even if it was a single python file that had one strenum in it. that could be read by an agent to see what its section name maps to, and at the same time used in the code to do the mapping. just one. width a note in the architecture that says, when adding sections here is how you add an agent, use this template, append to this enum, or dict, or struct... If there are alias names for sections to pick up deprecated or historic names of sections, then a second map can be added that says the different strings that might be used to represent 'fact_check' for example, 'Facts check', 'Fact Checker'.\\\"\\n\\nEvidence gathered this session: only 3 of the actually-used section names (fact_check, rt_ica, issue_classification, plus the special groomed key) are registered in plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/rendering.py's SECTION_HEADING dict. Confirmed independently hardcoded, unregistered section-name string literals in plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md (section=\\\"Fact-Check\\\"), rtica-assessor.md (section=\\\"RT-ICA\\\"), impact-analyst.md (section=\\\"Impact Radius\\\", plus Files/Output-Evidence/suggested_location referenced as expected sections), and backlog-item-groomer.md (writes ## Groomed via a separate groomed_content param). The #2956 bug report additionally names Resources, Impact, Dependencies, Priority, Benefits, Research, Design Intent Alignment, Acceptance Criteria, Expected Behavior as corrupted section names, none of which are registered. backlog_groom's MCP section parameter is a plain str with no Literal/enum validation at the boundary.\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-18T10:54:38.410829Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The system behaves as designed but the design is incomplete. Section names are passed to the MCP `backlog_groom` as unvalidated plain strings with no enum/Literal type constraint. Agents independently hardcode section-name strings in their markdown without consulting a shared registry. No validation gate exists at the write boundary to reject unregistered section names. The system allows invented names to silently accumulate, which is the underlying condition enabling the corruption observed in #2956 and #2974.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A \u2014 missing-guardrail classifications do not require root-cause analysis\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Agents independently inventing unregistered section names \u2192 Canonical registry enforced at write boundary with validation, alias-map support for deprecation, and stderr diagnostic on fallback-to-unknown__\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **no canonical section-name registry \u2014 grooming agents hardcode arbitrary section names independently** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 architecture review with user, 2026-08-18\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Investigation Update 2026 08 20\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verdict: RESOLVED.** Implemented by PR #2987 (commit `e9c1d72d`, \\\"canonical section-name registry with write-boundary validation\\\"), merged to `main` and confirmed an ancestor of current HEAD.\\n\\nEvidence checked against current source:\\n- `backlog_core/section_registry.py`: `SectionKey`/`SubsectionKey` StrEnums, `SECTION_HEADING`/`SECTION_NAME_ALIASES` dicts, `resolve_section_name()`/`resolve_subsection_name()` \u2014 a leaf module with no internal imports, importable by any caller without a cycle.\\n- Used identically by the write path (`operations.py`), read path (`rendering.py`), GitHub-parse path (`github_sync.py`), and the legacy `.md` parser (`parsing.py`).\\n- Alias map (`SECTION_NAME_ALIASES`) kept as a separate dict from the canonical enum, per the original spec.\\n- Documented convention for adding new sections lives in the module docstring and `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`.\\n- All hardcoded `section=\\\"...\\\"` literals swept across `plugins/development-harness/agents/*.md` and `skills/**/*.md` resolve to registered `SectionKey` display headings \u2014 none orphaned.\\n- Recursive subsection mirror (`SubsectionKey`, `SUBSECTION_NAME_ALIASES`, `resolve_subsection_name()`) exists and is wired into `github_sync._parse_groomed_section`.\\n- Write path always reduces to canonical form (`operations._normalize_section_key`); unregistered names emit an unconditional stderr diagnostic (`operations._warn_unregistered_section`) and are also recorded to `Output.warnings`.\\n- Normalize-on-read healing (`rendering.normalize_unknown_sections`) wired into both YAML load paths.\\n- Covered by `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_section_registry.py` (802 lines).\\n\\nClosing as resolved \u2014 this repo's convention (`fix-delegation-discipline.md`) deliberately omits `Fixes #N` trailers, so the merge did not auto-close this issue; closing manually now with the reference.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"bfaa01d742d65179e8330cade4917d630ae8fca573e400efbbc860984f2dce9e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPt1-7g\"}"}